      "name": "Arata Dodo | Taigan and the Photobook as a Form of Travel | Photo Coordinates",
      "description": "Arata Dodo photographs places where people live, from rapidly changing Shanghai to the five countries bordering the Caspian Sea, Ulaanbaatar, and Kyoto. In books including Ways of Shanghai, Taigan, and White Map on the Silk Road, he records urban change, borders, religion, resource industries, and family life through photographs that keep people and their surroundings in the same frame. His travel photography treats each destination as an inhabited present and incorporates his own judgment about what needs to be seen now, without turning distant places into specimens of cultural difference.",
