      "name": "Fabian Marti | Scanners, Photograms, and the Materiality of Photography | Photo Coordinates",
      "description": "Fabian Marti is a Swiss artist whose work moves across scanners, scratched negatives, photograms, appropriated images, ceramics, video, and installation. Dust and scratches on the scanning surface, drawing on negatives, and computer-generated forms returned to the darkroom leave visible traces of the machines and handwork through which the photographic image was made. Since the 2000s, Marti has used digital imagery as a meeting point for reproduction, chance, material processes, and mystical signs, retaining the residue that digital correction typically removes.",
